  "note": "Election of the Limavady Urban District Council, 18 May 1955; nine nominations for nine seats, returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1955, p. 6; Derry Journal, 6 May 1955, p. 5). Nine nominations for nine seats, so there was no contest. The Derry Journal reports the new council as eight Unionists and one Labour member; eight candidates were nominated by the local Unionist Association and the ninth, H. P. M'Laughlin, as a Labour representative. Six of the nine were members of the old council. No party label was printed beside every name in the News-Letter list, but the journal's count supports the labels shown. Returned unopposed."
